      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "MOVEHOME ESTATE AGENTS... are delighted to present a fantastic three bedroomed terraced home, spanning approx 883 sq ft and set in a private row of 17 houses tucked away off Russell Street to the open market. Behind the handsome red brick façade of this charming property, lies spacious proportions throughout with original features and ceiling covings. Built c.1890's, this really is a home of distinction which combines enormous character with a classic contemporary style and all the comforts and conveniences one could wish for.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises of a welcoming hallway, front living room, living/dining room, kitchen/dining area and downstairs bathroom. Upstairs consists of three bedrooms and a bathroom completes the accommodation on this level. There is ample storage throughout the property. Outside, the rear garden is accessed from the kitchen area, which is private, enclosed and very low maintenance. There is a private front space that is enclosed with railings and providing privacy from the street. The much anticipated release of this property to the market represents a rare and genuine opportunity to purchase a wonderful three bedroom terraced home set in a well established Dublin location.\r\n\r\nSt. Patricks Terrace is located close to the magnificent Croke Park Stadium just off Russell Street, Drumcondra. Several of Ireland’s most prestigious educational institutions are within walking distance, including St. Patrick’s College of Education, Mater Dei Institute of Education and All Hallows College, all 3 associated with nearby Dublin City University. Also, within a short distance are the IFSC, East Point Business Park and Drumcondra & Clontarf Station are within striking distance. There are also numerous bus routes and trains servicing Drumcondra and a wide selection of shops, boutique restaurants, public houses, churches, and cafes. The Russell Street bakery is the standout bakery on the street and is only 100 yards away. The Transport links available at Number 15 are unrivalled in the city. Drumcondra rail station is just 700 metres from the house with connections to Malahide and Bray (via Connolly and Grand Canal Dock), Sligo (via Maynooth and Longford), and all stations on the Cork/Galway/Limerick rail lines with services running via the Phoenix Park Tunnel. Drumcondra Station is a key stop on the planned DART+ West line, which will electrify the railway line from Dublin Connolly to Maynooth and the M3 Parkway.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is essential to appreciate all this wonderful property has to offer and by appointment with MOVEHOME ESTATE AGENTS - 01 8844690"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
